---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Why Does My Bra Band Feel Too Tight? Causes & Relief | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Discover why your bra band feels tight or constricting. Learn the backward band test to diagnose whether tight bands are caused by band size or small cups."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/fit-guide/band-too-tight"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Fit Guide', url: '/fit-guide' },
      { label: 'Band Too Tight' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Fit Diagnostic
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        Why Does My Bra Band Feel Too Tight?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        A band that leaves painful red marks or restricts breathing can ruin your day. However, a tight band is frequently caused by small cups rather than an undersized band.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <section class="bg-canvas-soft-2 border-2 border-primary/30 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">Quick Answer</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed font-medium">
          A bra band feels too tight either because <strong>the band size is physically too small</strong> or because <strong>the cups are too small</strong>, forcing breast tissue out into the band.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Possible Causes -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Plausible Causes</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">1. Small Cups Stealing Band Circumference</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">When cups cannot fit your breast volume, breast tissue pushes the cups forward, pulling the band taut around your back like a tourniquet.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">2. Underestimated Underbust Measurement</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Measuring underbust while breathing in or pulling the tape too tight can result in selecting a band size smaller than your ribcage structure.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">3. Brand & Fabric Stiffness</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">New unwashed bras or dark-dyed fabrics naturally run stiffer than worn light-colored bras.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What to Check: Backward Band Test -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Diagnostic: The Backward Band Test</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          To isolate whether the band or the cup is causing tightness:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>Put your bra on upside-down and backwards, so the cups hang down your back like a cape and the hook closure is at the front.</li>
          <li>Fasten the hooks on the loosest setting around your underbust.</li>
          <li><strong>Result A:</strong> If the band feels comfortable backwards, <em>your band size is correct and your cups are too small</em>.</li>
          <li><strong>Result B:</strong> If the band still feels tight backwards, <em>your band size is genuinely too small</em>.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <!-- Recommended Size Adjustment -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Recommended Size Adjustment</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">IF BACKWARD TEST WAS COMFORTABLE (RESULT A)</span>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Keep band size, increase cup letter (e.g. 34C &rarr; 34D)</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">IF BACKWARD TEST WAS TIGHT (RESULT B)</span>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Increase band size, decrease cup letter (e.g. 34C &rarr; 36B sister size)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Calculator CTA -->
      <section class="bg-primary text-white rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 text-center sm:text-left flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6 shadow-md">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">Calculate Your Baseline Size</h2>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-canvas-soft-2">Re-verify your underbust measurements in inches or centimeters.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/#calculator" class="flex-shrink-0 h-12 px-6 bg-surface hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm rounded-xl shadow-xs transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>Calculate My Size &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Related Fit Guides -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Related Fit Guides</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold">
          <a href="/fit-guide/band-rides-up" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Does My Bra Band Ride Up?</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide/underwire-digging" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Does My Bra Underwire Dig In?</a>
          <a href="/sister-size-calculator" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Sister Size Calculator</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Return to Fit Guide Hub</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
